Subject: Request: GPO evidence and CIS test servers – Qualys CIS Level 1 failures on Windows Server

Hi team,

Our Windows Servers score about 40% in the Qualys CIS Level 1 compliance scan (Qualys Cloud Agent). We need to find out whether the CIS settings are missing from our GPOs, whether the GPOs are not reaching the servers, or whether Qualys is evaluating incorrectly.

Parts A and B are read-only: nothing is changed. Part C needs test servers and can be raised as a separate change if required.
Please save all outputs to a single folder and attach them to this ticket. If something cannot be collected, just note why.

Example server: <SERVER NAME> (Windows Server 2022)

------------------------------------------------------------
PART A – Domain / GPO evidence (AD or GPO administrator)
Run on a domain controller or a management server with RSAT, in PowerShell as an account with read access to GPOs.

A1. OU of the server:
  Get-ADComputer <SERVER NAME> | Select-Object DistinguishedName | Out-File C:\temp\A1_server_OU.txt

A2. GPOs that apply to that OU, in precedence order (use the OU from A1):
  Get-GPInheritance -Target "<OU distinguished name from A1>" | Format-List * | Out-File C:\temp\A2_gpo_inheritance.txt
  (Get-GPInheritance -Target "<OU distinguished name from A1>").InheritedGpoLinks | Format-Table -AutoSize | Out-File -Append C:\temp\A2_gpo_inheritance.txt

A3. Settings report of all GPOs:
  Get-GPOReport -All -ReportType Html -Path C:\temp\A3_AllGPOs.html

A4. Effective result for the server, pulled remotely:
  Get-GPResultantSetOfPolicy -Computer <SERVER NAME> -ReportType Html -Path C:\temp\A4_<SERVER NAME>_rsop.html

A5. Backup of all GPOs (for comparison in Microsoft Policy Analyzer):
  mkdir C:\temp\A5_GPOBackup
  Backup-GPO -All -Path C:\temp\A5_GPOBackup
  Then zip the folder.

A6. Please also answer:
- Which GPO(s) are meant to harden member servers, and what baseline were they built from (CIS, Microsoft Security Baseline, in-house)? Which version?
- Do any of them use security filtering or WMI filters? If so, what do the filters target?
- Is inheritance blocked on any server OU, or are any links disabled or Enforced?

